{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377870-blurred-form-style-how-does-this-work","id":1377870,"title":"Blurred Form Style: How does this work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-01T20:31:12-07:00","id":1377870,"title":"Blurred Form Style: How does this work?","content":"I'm intensionally borrowing the title from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/994613-blurred-form-style-how-does-this-work\">this</a> thread, which unfortunately garnered no replies.<br /> <br /> The combat stealth rules being what they are, I want to make sure that I understand how this charm is meant to function. In particular, I'm hoping that people can explain this sentence &quot;Any time she attacks or changes range bands, se can be seen and targeted by opponents until her next turn in which she doesn't.&quot;<br /> <br /> Can I ask the forum to walk through how this would play out in combat for, say, a solar Ebon Shadow stylist? <br /> <br /> A fight happens. Our solar ninja uses Blinding Battle Feint to supplement the Join Battle roll and reflexively activates Blurred Form Style (or maybe it would make more sense to activate after her first attack from stealth?). How does the fight go from there? (What I'm really asking is when and how can she use Blurred Form Style to make attacks from stealth in combat.)<br /> <br /> Bonus question: is this charm good (especially given the cancel-on-hit condition)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T22:20:38-07:00","id":1377886,"title":"","content":"My character has the Charm, but not Ebon Shadow, so I don\u2019t have much to say in that regard. I use it, but not especially for combat; the (Essence) autosuccesses would surely help on that initial Join Battle roll, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T04:40:59-07:00","id":1377926,"title":"","content":"My reading of that would be that while the martist is not invisible, they do not gain the autosux from the style charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T06:17:46-07:00","id":1377938,"title":"","content":"Your first attack on the first turn is an unexpected attack, possibly an ambush, but then you\u2019re visible. If you want to be hidden again you can flurry your attack with a stealth attempt, but blurred form style isn\u2019t making you invisible so you need actual cover. If you have no cover then you need to wait until your next turn, where you can use your action to attempt to stealth again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T16:00:16-07:00","id":1380226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377870-blurred-form-style-how-does-this-work#post1377870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm intensionally borrowing the title from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/994613-blurred-form-style-how-does-this-work\">this</a> thread, which unfortunately garnered no replies.<br /> <br /> The combat stealth rules being what they are, I want to make sure that I understand how this charm is meant to function. In particular, I'm hoping that people can explain this sentence &quot;Any time she attacks or changes range bands, se can be seen and targeted by opponents until her next turn in which she doesn't.&quot;<br /> <br /> Can I ask the forum to walk through how this would play out in combat for, say, a solar Ebon Shadow stylist?<br /> <br /> A fight happens. Our solar ninja uses Blinding Battle Feint to supplement the Join Battle roll and reflexively activates Blurred Form Style (or maybe it would make more sense to activate after her first attack from stealth?). How does the fight go from there? (What I'm really asking is when and how can she use Blurred Form Style to make attacks from stealth in combat.)<br /> <br /> Bonus question: is this charm good (especially given the cancel-on-hit condition)?</div> </div> </div> </div>It allows you to take stealth in ways that aren't really feasible in combat: By staying put. <br /> <br /> It does work, though. You stop, you disappear, and everyone has to roll stealth and awareness accordingly. It's just that people still know where you are, since you had to stop completely. Nothing's stopping them from attacking you blindly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}